* CT07/T2 U4-A early feasibility screen (candidate-only; not U5 evidence).
* The 1:1000 transfer, burden, SRF, DCR, parasitics, temperature, and
* waveform knobs are explicit so a failed screen rejects the candidate rather
* than being hidden by nominal CST3015 arithmetic.
.title CT07-1000 candidate threshold and bandwidth screen
.param CT_RATIO=1000
.param R_BURDEN=4.02
.param R_TOL=0.01
.param C_FILTER=1n
.param R_FILTER=100
.param L_MAG=1.2m
.param R_DCR=18
.param L_LEAK=8u
.param C_PAR=45p
.param TEMP_C=25
.param VCC=3.3
.param VREF=2.048
.param R_REF_TOP=75k
.param R_REF_BOTTOM=10k
.param THRESHOLD_A=60
.param SOURCE_RMS_A=15
.param FAULT_A=60
.param HARMONIC_FRACTION=0.30
.param ASYMMETRY_FRACTION=0.08
.param COMPARATOR_DELAY_NS=80
.param LATCH_DELAY_NS=120
.param CLOCK_UNCERTAINTY_NS=25

* Primary current contains 35 kHz content and a deliberately asymmetric
* component.  The threshold crossing is on the calibrated primary current,
* not a secondary/comparator node.
* Behavioral current sources keep the transfer ratio explicit while the
* inductance/DCR/leakage/parasitic network remains available for screening.
BFAULT primary 0 I={FAULT_A*(1+HARMONIC_FRACTION*sin(2*pi*35k*time)+ASYMMETRY_FRACTION*sin(2*pi*17.5k*time))}
LPRIMARY primary 0 {L_MAG}
BSECOND sense_raw 0 I={FAULT_A*(1+HARMONIC_FRACTION*sin(2*pi*35k*time)+ASYMMETRY_FRACTION*sin(2*pi*17.5k*time))/CT_RATIO}
R_DCR sense_raw secondary_model {R_DCR}
LLEAK secondary_model 0 {L_LEAK}
CPAR secondary_model 0 {C_PAR}
RBURDEN sense_raw reference {R_BURDEN*(1+R_TOL)}
RFILTER sense_raw filtered {R_FILTER}
CFILTER filtered reference {C_FILTER}
VREF reference 0 {VREF}
BTRIP comparator 0 V={if(V(filtered)>=V(reference)*R_REF_BOTTOM/(R_REF_TOP+R_REF_BOTTOM),VCC,0)}
RDELAY comparator latch_in 1
CDELAY latch_in 0 {COMPARATOR_DELAY_NS*1n/1.65}
BLATCH latch 0 V={if(V(latch_in)>1.65,VCC,0)}

.tran 1n 100u
.meas tran sense_max MAX V(filtered)
.meas tran sense_min MIN V(filtered)
.meas tran comparator_max MAX V(comparator)
.meas tran latch_max MAX V(latch)
.end
